alforge (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: a browser-launched install was silent when it failed. Errors such as
    "no .deb asset in this release", an unknown repository or a malformed URI
    went to stderr, which the browser discards. They now raise a zenity/kdialog
    error box, and a successful install (or an up-to-date check) shows a short
    pop-up, so the button always answers.

 -- dubiduglitch <dubiduglitch@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0000

alforge (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Browser integration: register the alforge:// URI scheme with a .desktop
    file, and ship a content script that adds an "Install with alforge" button
    to GitHub, GitLab and Codeberg project pages (the GNOME-Look model).
  * New internal 'handle-uri' command: resolves the target, shows the exact
    artifact in a zenity/kdialog confirmation, and installs only on approval.
    Only forge targets are accepted, never a direct .deb URL.
  * --dry-run now prints the apt command it would run instead of reporting a
    successful installation.
  * Fix Codeberg: 'codeberg:owner/repo' and pasted codeberg.org URLs failed with
    "codeberg expects 'host/owner/repo'". The host is implied again, and a
    lookalike host is no longer accepted.

 -- dubiduglitch <dubiduglitch@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:20:00 +0000

alforge (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Follow the newest stable release: a pre-release is skipped in favour of the
    latest stable one, with a new --allow-prerelease flag to opt into betas.
  * Reuse a previously verified artifact from the download cache instead of
    re-downloading it on every --download-only run or download-mode timer tick.
  * Take a per-user write lock so a timer run and a manual upgrade cannot
    interleave and clobber the registry or state.
  * Report "not installed" together with the available version after a
    download-only run.

 -- dubiduglitch <dubiduglitch@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:50:00 +0000

alforge (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging.
  * Multi-forge .deb package manager with systemd --user timer support.

